window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-74fe0a93ace90e8b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"refactor-your-codebase\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">重构代码库</h1> <p>清理无用代码、更新旧模式，同时保持现有行为不变。</p> <p>让 Codex 删除无用代码、梳理过大的文件、合并重复逻辑，并以小而易审查的步骤更新陈旧模式。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>存在无用代码、过大的模块、重复逻辑或陈旧抽象，导致日常修改成本过高的代码库。</li> <li>需要在原有代码库中逐步现代化，而不是借机迁移框架或技术栈的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/security-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$security-best-practices（需联网）</a></td> <td>在合并之前，审查与安全相关的清理、依赖项更改、身份验证流程和对外暴露的界面。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.system/skill-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$skill-creator（需联网）</a></td> <td>将验证过的现代化模式、审查清单或一致性检查流程制作为可重复使用的代码库技能或团队技能。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>分小步进行现代化改造</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请对这个代码库进行现代化改造和重构。\n\n要求：\n\n- 除非我明确要求更改功能，否则请保持现有行为。\n\n- 先找出正在拖慢修改速度的问题：无用代码、重复路径、过大的模块、陈旧抽象和旧模式。\n\n- 对于每个拟议步骤，说明当前行为、结构上的改进，以及用于证明行为保持稳定的验证检查。\n\n- 将工作拆分成易审查的小型重构步骤，例如删除无用代码、简化控制流、提取辅助函数，或依据代码库当前约定替换过时模式。\n\n- 除非重构确实要求修改，否则保持公开 API 稳定。\n\n- 指出应拆分为独立迁移任务的框架迁移、依赖项升级、API 更改或架构调整。\n\n- 如果工作范围较大，请提出在实施前应创建的文档、规范和行为一致性检查。\n\n请先提出计划。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用 Codex 现代化改造代码库（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>如果代码库中积累了无用代码、重复逻辑、陈旧抽象、过大的文件或旧模式，导致每次更改的成本都越来越高，就应考虑通过重构减少工程债务。重构的目标是改善现有系统的结构，而不是借机迁移技术栈。</p> <p>Codex 可以先梳理杂乱的部分，再通过一系列便于审查的小步骤完成整理：删除无用路径、梳理过大的模块、合并重复路径、更新过时的框架模式，并为每一步加强验证。</p> <p>目标是在当前代码库中完成改进：</p> <ol> <li>删除不再需要的无用代码、陈旧辅助函数、旧标志和兼容性垫片。</li> <li>通过提取辅助函数、拆分组件或将副作用移到更清晰的边界，缩减臃肿的模块。</li> <li>根据代码库当前的约定替换旧模式：使用较新的框架原语、更清晰的类型、更简单的状态流，或标准库工具。</li> <li>保持公开行为稳定，同时降低后续更改的成本。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>编辑之前，先让 Codex 梳理目标区域：臃肿模块、重复逻辑、无用代码、测试、公开契约，以及代码库已不再适用的旧模式。</li> <li>每次只选择一种整理目标：删除无用代码、简化控制流、更新过时模式，或将大文件拆分为边界明确的小文件。</li> <li>在 Codex 修改文件之前，让它说明当前行为、计划进行的结构改进，以及最小的稳定性验证方式。</li> <li>每一步之后都审查并运行最有用的小型检查，不要将全部清理工作一次性塞进一个差异中。</li> <li>除非完成整理确有必要，否则将技术栈更改、依赖项迁移和架构调整作为独立任务处理。</li> </ol> <p>你可以使用 Plan 模式，在开始重构之前先制定计划。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-execplans\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"execplans\">使用 ExecPlans</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">代码现代化改造 Cookbook</a>介绍了 ExecPlans：它是一类文档，可用于概述整理工作的目标状态，并记录每一步的验证结果。</p> <p>如果重构涉及多个模块或需要多个会话，ExecPlans 会很有用。你可以用它记录已删除的内容、更新的模式、必须保持不变的契约，以及仍待处理的事项。</p> <p><a id=\"use-skills-for-repeatable-patterns\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">使用技能复用重复模式</h2> <p>如果相同的整理规则在多个代码库、服务或团队中反复出现，<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能（Skills）（本地尚未收录）</a>就很有用。可以使用特定框架的技能；对于风险较高的整理工作，还可以增加安全和 CI 技能。如果已形成可靠的检查清单，也可以创建团队技能，用于复用无用代码清理、模块拆分或行为一致性检查流程。</p> <p>如果你在多个代码库中重复进行同一种现代化改造，Codex 可以帮助你将第一次成功的流程整理成可复用技能。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"refactor-your-codebase\">Refactor your codebase</h1> <p>Remove dead code and modernize legacy patterns without changing behavior.</p> <p>Use Codex to remove dead code, untangle large files, collapse duplicated logic, and modernize stale patterns in small reviewable passes.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Codebases with dead code, oversized modules, duplicated logic, or stale abstractions that make routine edits expensive.</li> <li>Teams that need to modernize code in place without turning the work into a framework or stack migration.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/security-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$security-best-practices (online)</a></td> <td>Review security-sensitive cleanup, dependency changes, auth flows, and exposed surfaces before merging a modernization pass.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.system/skill-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$skill-creator (online)</a></td> <td>Turn a proven modernization pattern, review checklist, or parity workflow into a reusable repo or team skill.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Modernize in Small Passes</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Modernize and refactor this codebase.\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve behavior unless I explicitly ask for a functional change.\n- Start by identifying dead code, duplicated paths, oversized modules, stale abstractions, and legacy patterns that are slowing changes down.\n- For each proposed pass, name the current behavior, the structural improvement, and the validation check that should prove behavior stayed stable.\n- Break the work into small reviewable refactor passes such as deleting dead code, simplifying control flow, extracting helpers, or replacing outdated patterns with the repo's current conventions.\n- Keep public APIs stable unless a change is required by the refactor.\n- Call out any framework migration, dependency upgrade, API change, or architecture move that should be split into a separate migration task.\n- If the work is broad, propose the docs, specs, and parity checks we should create before implementation.\n\nPropose a plan to do this.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Modernizing your Codebase with Codex (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When your codebase has accumulated unused code, duplicated logic, stale abstractions, large files, or legacy patterns that make every change more expensive than it should be, you should consider reducing the engineering debt with a refactor. Refactoring is about improving the shape of the existing system without turning it into a stack migration.</p> <p>Codex is useful here because it can first map the messy area, then land the cleanup in small reviewable passes: deleting unused paths, untangling large modules, collapsing duplicate paths, modernizing old framework patterns, and tightening validation around each pass.</p> <p>The goal is to improve the current codebase in place:</p> <ol> <li>Remove unused code, stale helpers, old flags, and compatibility shims that are no longer needed.</li> <li>Shrink noisy modules by extracting helpers, splitting components, or moving side effects to clearer boundaries.</li> <li>Replace legacy patterns with the repo's current conventions: newer framework primitives, clearer types, simpler state flow, or standard library utilities.</li> <li>Keep public behavior stable while making the next change cheaper.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Ask Codex to map the area before editing: noisy modules, duplicated logic, unused code, tests, public contracts, and any old patterns that the repo has outgrown.</li> <li>Pick one cleanup theme at a time: remove unused code, simplify control flow, modernize an outdated pattern, or split a large file into smaller owned pieces.</li> <li>Before Codex patches files, have it state the current behavior, the structural improvement it wants to make, and the smallest check that should prove behavior stayed stable.</li> <li>Review and run the smallest useful check after each pass instead of batching the whole cleanup into one diff.</li> <li>Keep stack changes, dependency migrations, and architecture moves as separate tasks unless they're required to finish the cleanup.</li> </ol> <p>You can use Plan mode to create a plan for the refactor before starting the work.</p> <h2 id=\"leverage-execplans\">Leverage ExecPlans</h2> <p>The <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/codex/code_modernization.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">code modernization cookbook</a> introduces ExecPlans: documents that let Codex keep an overview of the cleanup, spell out the intended end state, and log validation after each pass. They're useful when the refactor spans more than one module or takes more than one session. Use them to record deletions, pattern updates, contracts that had to stay stable, and what's still deferred.</p> <h2 id=\"use-skills-for-repeatable-patterns\">Use skills for repeatable patterns</h2> <p><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Skills (not in this local snapshot)</a> are useful when the same cleanup rules repeat across repos, services, or teams. Use framework-specific skills when available, add security and CI skills around risky cleanups, and create a team skill when you have a proven checklist for unused-code removal, module extraction, or legacy-pattern modernization. If you end up doing the same modernization pass across more than one codebase, Codex can help turn the first successful pass into a reusable skill.</p>"};
